" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/53/465453/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I85a3e96b69fc6229d29c87a6e4a01f77f75aa855" commit="70982714faf1fa119cde66ad9ea342351d4a807d" commit_message="BACKPORT: [media] mtk-vcodec: use V4L2_DEC_CMD_STOP to implement flush  Also remove the code using size-0 OUTPUT buffer to flush.  Signed-off-by: Tiffany Lin &lt;tiffany.lin@mediatek.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Wu-Cheng Li &lt;wuchengli@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kuang-che Wu &lt;kcwu@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Mauro Carvalho Chehab &lt;mchehab@s-opensource.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 4865fffa834884ffc49a551bb3c7ac8a76e8585d) Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; [djkurtz: chromeos-4.4 does not have commit d6dd645eae76 (&quot;[media] media:  videobuf2: Move timestamp to vb2_buffer&quot;).  So, the timestamp field in  still in struct vb2_v4l2_buffer not struct vb2_buffer.]  BUG=b:35647990 TEST=build and boot rowan to UI and confirm youtube uses HW Decode  Change-Id: I85a3e96b69fc6229d29c87a6e4a01f77f75aa855 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/465454 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wu-cheng Li &lt;wuchengli@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="465454" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/54/465454/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I84120ec73fcb5d493cfc1d66ca530b0dd796326b" commit="547f197493e977020a0f1f99085758790c9e4780" commit_message="UPSTREAM: [media] mtk-vcodec: fix build warnings without DEBUG  After removing DEBUG from mtk_vcodec_util.h, some build warnings are generated as the following: .../drivers/media/platform/mtk-vcodec/vdec_vpu_if.c: In function 'vcodec_vpu_send_msg': .../drivers/media/platform/mtk-vcodec/vdec_vpu_if.c:73:11: warning: unused variable 'msg_id' [-Wunused-variable]   uint32_t msg_id = *(uint32_t *)msg;            ^ .../drivers/media/platform/mtk-vcodec/mtk_vcodec_dec.c: In function 'vb2ops_vdec_buf_queue': .../drivers/media/platform/mtk-vcodec/mtk_vcodec_dec.c:1129:7: warning: unused variable 'log_level' [-Wunused-variable]    int log_level = ret ? 0 : 1;        ^ .../drivers/media/platform/mtk-vcodec/venc_vpu_if.c: In function 'vpu_enc_send_msg': .../drivers/media/platform/mtk-vcodec/venc_vpu_if.c:82:12: warning: unused variable 'msg_id' [-Wunused-variable]    uint32_t msg_id = *(uint32_t *)msg;             ^  It is because mtk_vcodec_debug() and mtk_vcodec_err() are defined as empty macros. Without DEBUG definition, the variable for debugging is not used anymore. Fixing build warnings by moving the assignment of the variable to the argument of mtk_vcodec_debug() and mtk_vcodec_err(). Within the patch, build pass with/without DEBUG definition, and functions still work fine.  Signed-off-by: Minghsiu Tsai &lt;minghsiu.tsai@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Mauro Carvalho Chehab &lt;mchehab@s-opensource.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 9eeb0ed0f30938f31a3d9135a88b9502192c18dd) Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=b:35647990 TEST=build and boot rowan to UI and confirm youtube uses HW Decode  Change-Id: I84120ec73fcb5d493cfc1d66ca530b0dd796326b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/465455 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wu-cheng Li &lt;wuchengli@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="465455" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/55/465455/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I409591ae732fd2a0c99e1f4ee8463e2aac75e4fd" commit="3d0e076a7970e96851213f366828f16e3f5994a6" commit_message="Chameleon: Add flow manager  Add flow manager for backward compatible flow based APIs. Don't let chameleon driver access flow devices directly. Especially for init and reset things. Hide the logic from driver. The flow manager also takes responsibility for checking if the flow exists or not.  BUG=chromium:567364 TEST=make remote-install to make sure Chameleon is booted successfully. Verified display_Resolution.mirrored with HDMI on ELM. Verified audio_AudioBasicHDMI with HDMI on ELM. Test if we can record audio from LineIn.  Change-Id: I409591ae732fd2a0c99e1f4ee8463e2aac75e4fd Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/459577 Commit-Ready: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="459577" owner_email="mojahsu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/chameleon" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/chameleon" ref="refs/changes/77/459577/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8fb0f0d8f234fa476168dcea5f2bcf124ec5bfc6" commit="acfb5858759eaa775dfbc070993cb2249a48e7ed" commit_message="chameleon: Add a device manager  Add a device manager for future integration.  BUG=chromium:567364 TEST=make remote-install to make sure Chameleon is booted successfully.  Change-Id: I8fb0f0d8f234fa476168dcea5f2bcf124ec5bfc6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/459464 Commit-Ready: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wai-Hong Ta